<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Migration on Berrytree.org</title><link>https://berrytree.org/tags/migration/</link><description>Recent content in Migration on Berrytree.org</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="https://berrytree.org/tags/migration/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Chapter V: Wagons South</title><link>https://berrytree.org/books/wagons-south-wagons-west/ch05-wagons-south/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://berrytree.org/books/wagons-south-wagons-west/ch05-wagons-south/</guid><description>&lt;div class="ancestor-page"&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;header class="book-banner" role="banner"&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="https://berrytree.org/books/wagons-south-wagons-west/"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="book-banner-title"&gt;Wagons South and Wagons West&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="book-banner-author"&gt;by Glenn Berry&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/header&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="book-chapter-nav"&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://berrytree.org/books/wagons-south-wagons-west/ch04-the-revolutionary-war/"&gt;← Chapter IV: The Revolutionary War&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href="https://berrytree.org/books/wagons-south-wagons-west/"&gt;Table of Contents&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href="https://berrytree.org/books/wagons-south-wagons-west/ch06-away-down-south-in-dixie/"&gt;Chapter VI: Away Down South in Dixie →&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="chapter-v"&gt;Chapter V&lt;a class="anchor" href="#chapter-v"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="wagons-south--alabama--heart-of-dixie"&gt;Wagons South — Alabama — &amp;ldquo;Heart of Dixie&amp;rdquo;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#wagons-south--alabama--heart-of-dixie"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="a-state-of-alabama-created-december-14-1819"&gt;A. State of Alabama created December 14, 1819&lt;a class="anchor" href="#a-state-of-alabama-created-december-14-1819"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Some native-born Americans from the 13 Original Colonies trickled into Alabama while the British ruled here. After the Revolutionary War ended, the trickle became an increasing stream&amp;hellip;A boundary dispute with Spain involving Alabama was settled by the Treaty of San Lorenzo 1795. (&lt;a href="https://berrytree.org/books/wagons-south-wagons-west/bibliography/#ref-I"&gt;I; p.123&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Chapter IX: Texas Fever in the Air</title><link>https://berrytree.org/books/wagons-south-wagons-west/ch09-texas-fever-in-the-air/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://berrytree.org/books/wagons-south-wagons-west/ch09-texas-fever-in-the-air/</guid><description>&lt;div class="ancestor-page"&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;header class="book-banner" role="banner"&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="https://berrytree.org/books/wagons-south-wagons-west/"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="book-banner-title"&gt;Wagons South and Wagons West&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="book-banner-author"&gt;by Glenn Berry&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/header&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="book-chapter-nav"&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://berrytree.org/books/wagons-south-wagons-west/ch08-i-wish-i-was-in-dixie/"&gt;← Chapter VIII: I Wish I Was in Dixie&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href="https://berrytree.org/books/wagons-south-wagons-west/"&gt;Table of Contents&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href="https://berrytree.org/books/wagons-south-wagons-west/ch10-in-dixie-land-where-i-was-born/"&gt;Chapter X: In Dixie Land Where I Was Born →&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="chapter-ix"&gt;Chapter IX&lt;a class="anchor" href="#chapter-ix"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="texas-fever-in-the-air"&gt;Texas Fever in the Air&lt;a class="anchor" href="#texas-fever-in-the-air"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;During the 1830&amp;rsquo;s and from thence onward, &amp;ldquo;Texas Fever&amp;rdquo; caught hold of many Alabamians. Many pioneers left the State of Alabama and County of Fayette before they had very deep roots established there.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Chapter XI: Look Away Dixie Land</title><link>https://berrytree.org/books/wagons-south-wagons-west/ch11-look-away-dixie-land/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://berrytree.org/books/wagons-south-wagons-west/ch11-look-away-dixie-land/</guid><description>&lt;div class="ancestor-page"&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;header class="book-banner" role="banner"&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="https://berrytree.org/books/wagons-south-wagons-west/"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="book-banner-title"&gt;Wagons South and Wagons West&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="book-banner-author"&gt;by Glenn Berry&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/header&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="book-chapter-nav"&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://berrytree.org/books/wagons-south-wagons-west/ch10-in-dixie-land-where-i-was-born/"&gt;← Chapter X: In Dixie Land Where I Was Born&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href="https://berrytree.org/books/wagons-south-wagons-west/"&gt;Table of Contents&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="chapter-xi"&gt;Chapter XI&lt;a class="anchor" href="#chapter-xi"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="look-away-dixie-land-1850-1860"&gt;&amp;hellip;Look Away Dixie Land&amp;hellip; (1850-1860)&lt;a class="anchor" href="#look-away-dixie-land-1850-1860"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The Federal Census of Fayette County Alabama 1850 reveals that there are eleven (11) of the BERRY surname as Head of Household. They are given below:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>